// Regression: RiskyDamageBoost and RecklessDashDoubledBolts must be cleared when
// RecklessDash is not in ActiveProtocols.
//
// Contract: the RecklessDash protocol owns RiskyDamageBoost (per-bolt component)
// and RecklessDashDoubledBolts (per-node resource). Both must be absent when
// RecklessDash is not active. Any code path that removes RecklessDash from
// ActiveProtocols MUST remove the component from all bolts and clear the resource.
//
// This scenario exercises the normal RecklessDash lifecycle under chaos input:
//   — RecklessDash is injected at frame 10 via InjectProtocol.
//   — Chaos input drives dash bumps, populating RiskyDamageBoost on the bolt and
//     RecklessDashDoubledBolts entries via the reckless_dash_on_bump and
//     reckless_dash_double_penalty systems.
//   — Node exits trigger reckless_dash_cleanup_node which must clear both.
//   — RecklessDashOrphaned asserts both are absent whenever RecklessDash is absent
//     from ActiveProtocols.
//
// Failure mode this protects against:
//   If reckless_dash_cleanup_node misses bolt entities on node exit (e.g. query
//   filtering issue) or RecklessDashDoubledBolts is not reset, the orphaned boost
//   component persists and misattributes damage multipliers on future cell impacts.
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Scatter",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.7)),
    max_frames: 3000,
    disallowed_failures: [
        NoNaN,
        BoltInBounds,
        BreakerInBounds,
        BoltSpeedAccurate,
        ValidDashState,
        BreakerCountReasonable,
        NoEntityLeaks,
        BoltCountReasonable,
        RecklessDashOrphaned,
    ],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    seed: 7253,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectProtocol(kind_name: "RecklessDash")),
    ],
)
